Package: heka-ghostd
Version: @VERSION@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Eric Polerecky <ghost@heka.dev>
Depends: pipewire, wireplumber, pipewire-pulse | pulseaudio-utils, libportaudio2, systemd, libc6 (>= 2.34)
Recommends: heka-ghost-desktop
Homepage: https://github.com/heka-vault/ghost
Description: Ghost voice assistant daemon
 Always-on, local-first voice assistant for one Linux workstation. Listens for
 "Hey Ghost" with local speech models, talks to an Anthropic-compatible model,
 and acts through the operator's MCP servers behind an audited write gate whose
 autonomy you set per operation. Ships a bundled Python runtime under /opt/ghost;
 speech models download on first run.
